Bluesky data
  Posts are read live from Bluesky's public Jetstream service and checked
  against the public Bluesky AppView (public.api.bsky.app). Post content
  belongs to its authors. Murmuration shows public posts only, stores none of
  them, and skips accounts that ask not to be shown to logged-out viewers.

Inspiration
  The 2007 Twingly Screensaver, which showed blog posts appearing on a
  spinning globe. No Twingly code or assets are used.
